  "answer": "### Short Answer\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThe controlling authority for this provision is Section 51 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), as amended.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor taxpayers, this means that the obligations to file income tax returns as specified in Section 51 remain in effect. Individuals must continue to comply with these requirements unless further amendments specifically alter these provisions. Tax practitioners should ensure that clients are aware of their filing obligations under this section, as it continues to govern individual income tax return requirements.",
